{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:OrganicChemistry.MolecularHopfRing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"OrganicChemistry.MolecularHopfRing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Parity","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Nat"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.weight_lt_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.weight_lt_chain","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L54-L64","doc":"The ring's reduced Alexander weight (linking number) is strictly less than the chain's\nfor N ≥ 4. This means the ring is energetically more efficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.alexanderWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.alexanderWeight","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L50-L52","doc":"reduced Alexander weight (linking number) of the ring (at q=1) is N/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.length","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L46-L48","doc":"Number of atoms in the ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.threading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.threading","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The threading link binding the ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.MolecularHopfRing","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L40-L44","doc":"A molecular Hopf ring: N atoms bound by a threading link T(2,N). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:molecular-hopf-ring","label":"def:molecular-hopf-ring","md":"quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.alexanderWeightAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.alexanderWeightAtOne","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L33-L38","doc":"reduced Alexander weight (linking number) of T(2,2m) at q=1 is m = N/2 (mirror of the\ncanonical `QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.alexanderWeightAtOne`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms_ge","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/molecular-hopf-ring.lean#L31-L31","doc":"At least 3 atoms for a ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms"